  "notes": "きつい is an i-adjective with a wide range of meanings from physical tightness to emotional harshness.\n\nFORMS:\n- Adverb: きつく\n- Noun form: きつさ\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{服|ふく}→服：00695_fuku⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧きつい: clothes are tight\n- ⟦{坂|さか}→坂：01415_saka⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧きつい: the slope is steep/demanding\n- ⟦{性格|せいかく}→性格：03371_seikaku⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧きつい: personality is harsh\n- ⟦{仕事|しごと}→仕事：00480_shigoto⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧きつい: work is tough/demanding\n- きつい⟦{言|い}い{方|かた}→言い方：14165_iikata⟧: harsh way of speaking\n- ⟦{匂|にお}い→匂い：00874_nioi⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧きつい: smell is strong/overpowering\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- きつい vs. ⟦{厳|きび}しい→厳しい：01125_kibishii⟧: きつい emphasizes difficulty or discomfort; ⟦{厳|きび}しい→厳しい：01125_kibishii⟧ emphasizes strictness or severity",
